  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best multimodal config (config_039: scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieves only 0.520 accuracy vs 0.514 for RNA-only, and notably has a worse F1 (0.479 vs 0.498), suggesting the weighted fusion may be diluting useful RNA signal with image noise. Question: config_009 is a single-variable ablation of config_039, changing only fusion from weighted to concat while keeping scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, and multiprofile fixed. This directly tests whether the fusion mechanism is the bottleneck preventing the image modality from contributing meaningfully. Why this is the best next experiment: With only 2 data points and a very small accuracy gap, the highest-priority uncertainty is whether the current multimodal pipeline can be made to clearly outperform the RNA-only baseline. Isolating the fusion choice (the most tunable hyperparameter in the fusion step) is the most information-dense single experiment. If concat improves accuracy and F1, it validates the multimodal direction and guides remaining budget toward concat-based variants; if it doesn't, it shifts focus to image encoder or RNA encoder choices."
}

